# title: SOUL DUEL
# SOUL DUEL sources in compile order, relative to this directory (the engine's come first, see
# engine/MANIFEST). Order matters: macros, structs, components and special variables before their
# users. tuning / rules / control / learn / kit are plain CL (host-tested); yama / ken / rukia / ichigo are the characters
# (data + hooks + cinematics); fighter ... main are the generic systems (no character names, except gate.lisp's pacing companions and debug.lisp's test scenarios).
# scripted.lisp (the learning / ASSIST gates' scripted players: ai.lisp calls them from the sim) loads right before ai.lisp.
# ken-meter / rukia-meter (Kenpachi's NOME / UDE, Rukia's cold gauge: each meter's step, reached by the kit's :tick hook, and its
# HUD widgets, the meter's :draw / :label) load right after hud.lisp: they use components' CLOG and hud's HUD-TEXT.
# senjumaru.lisp loads after hud / onehand: its HUD meter calls their functions (hud-text ...); the quad drawing macros are the engine's (ui.lisp), docs/duel/DUEL_SENJUMARU.md.
# Lille's art loads after senjumaru.lisp: lille-art (bodies, props) / lille-clips / lille-draw / lille-cine (Lille's shared art and
# cinematics), then barro-art (clips) / barro-draw / barro-stills, barro.lisp and barro-ai.lisp (Lille, kit :barro, roster index 6:
# index 5 is the removed old Lille's slot, docs/duel/DUEL_LILLE_V3.md): the roster is append-only.
# hisagi.lisp / hisagi-ai.lisp, then hisagi-art / hisagi-draw / hisagi-cine / hisagi-stills (Hisagi, kit :hisagi, roster index 7,
# docs/duel/DUEL_HISAGI.md) after Lille's. A character's files all carry its prefix (<name>.lisp the kit, <name>-ai the CPU, <name>-art
# the clips, <name>-draw / -cine / -stills by role).
